  "_comment": "🧩️ This subset's own contribution. The mutation vocabulary belongs to ONE subset of ONE standard of ONE artifact, so the (non-)oracle registration and the catalog live here. `s.architect.program` is a semio-NATIVE artifact persisted as `.dsl.semio` text and `.pack.semio` binary through this subset's own codecs; no third party reads or writes either, so no oracle is registered — see noOracleDecisions below.",
  "oracles": [],
  "noOracleDecisions": [
    {
      "id": "architect-program-mutation-semantics",
      "capabilities": [
        "program-1-mutate"
      ],
      "rationale": "No third-party library reads or writes semio's own `.dsl.semio`/`.pack.semio` envelope, and none is authoritative over an architectural BRIEF vocabulary in the first place: the 266 kinds are mechanically derived from this subset's own 66 registers by `📓️derivation-rules.md` — every header-shaped id-keyed register yields create/delete/rename/replace (rule 2), the two edge-shaped registers (`adjacencies`, `traces`) yield connect/disconnect instead (rule 4), and the three document-level scalar facets (`meta`, `project`, `governance`) yield rename/replace (rule 1). That derivation is a specification, not a fact an external library could confirm or refute. What stands in its place is the committed, independently handcrafted `(before, mutation, after, diff, outcome)` specification vector under each of the 266 `🧬️mutations/<slug>/🧪️tests/<fixture>/` leaves — 260 of which move the document — plus the inverse law as a metamorphic property: applying a kind and then its OWN computed inverse must restore the exact pre-mutation vector.",
      "substitutes": [
        "specification-vectors",
        "metamorphic-laws"
      ]
    }
  ],
